      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fairview never incorporated, yet a tight-knit community formed around the Fairview School, the town’s original gathering spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dlg.usg.edu/record/dlg_ghm_fairview",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The school, once called Mitchem's School, was built on land donated by the Mitchem family, who gave the community its first classroom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dlg.usg.edu/record/dlg_ghm_fairview",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early Fairview supported a sawmill and two cotton gins, keeping the local economy alive long before any commercial center appeared.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dlg.usg.edu/record/dlg_ghm_fairview",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cotton farms gave way to dairy pasture, turning Fairview’s landscape into a patchwork of pastures and small dairies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dlg.usg.edu/record/dlg_ghm_fairview",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Pierce, a prominent Atlanta dairy operator, opened a branch in Fairview, cementing the town’s role in regional dairy production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dlg.usg.edu/record/dlg_ghm_fairview",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "On its bicentennial, Morgan County erected a historical marker in Fairview to honor the community’s enduring legacy.",
